# Static chat UI

Single HTML file, no CSS/JS framework. Header / scrollable chat / footer. Chat (`#chat`) grows; header and footer hug their content.

## Mobile chrome

On viewports ~360–480px the composer MUST stay compact. Do not leave a large empty gap between the farewell hint and the input.

`flex-basis` follows the flex direction. A value meant as **width** in a row (`flex: 1 1 12rem`) becomes **height** if the same rule sits on a column. Override it in the column media query (`flex: 0 0 auto` or drop the basis).

```css
/* ❌ BAD — 12rem is height once the toolbar is a column */
.toolbar span { flex: 1 1 12rem; }
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .toolbar { flex-direction: column; }
}

/* ✅ GOOD */
.toolbar span { flex: 1 1 12rem; min-width: 0; }
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .toolbar { flex-direction: column; }
  .toolbar span { flex: 0 0 auto; }
}
```

Keep footer padding and toolbar gaps tight on small screens. Prefer wrapping or stacking controls over hiding the farewell hint or “Nueva consulta”.
